 "notes": "Limit from MeerKAT time-domain observations of PSR J2144-3933 (Battye et al.). Curve digitised from Fig. 7 (new_limit_plot.png in the e-print): 2-sigma (~95% CL) upper limit on g_agamma vs axion mass for the fiducial parallax distance D=0.165 kpc, computed as the highest upper limit over the pulsar-geometry region |beta|<4 deg, alpha>20 deg. Headline quote: g_agamma < 5.5e-11 GeV^-1 over 3.9-4.7 ueV. Paper assumes rho_DM = 0.45 GeV/cm^3, identical to the canonical value, so no rescaling applied. Gaps in the curve (e.g. 3.78-3.93 ueV) are RFI-excised frequency channels. Digitisation via colour extraction of the raster figure; per-column mean of the noisy trace, so rapid vertical excursions are slightly smoothed (full trace spans ~4.9-5.6e-11).",
